// The secret the far site's host proves its key with, as a model of `Secrets`.
//
// A site's file names its secret and never holds it. The host reads the value
// through a model of its own. The secret stays in the hosting process, out of
// every file a deployment shares.
//
// `gandr host --secrets` given this file applies `Secrets.secret` to the
// site's secret name. The answer is a sealed `Secret.T`. The host reads it
// whole, and no run prints it or ships it to a world. This model answers every
// name with the two-process test's host secret, which proves the far site's
// key.
//
// - see: `two-processes.site.gandr` — the site naming the secret `far`
// - see: `library/std/src/secret.gandr` — `Secret` and `Secrets`
// - see: `crates/surface-driver/tests/net.rs` — the host reading it

// The secret theory, from `std.secret` by its path.
import "../../../library/std/src/secret.gandr";

/// The far host's secrets: one for every name.
pub module Secrets : Model(Secrets) with sort K = Secret.T {
  /// The test host's secret, 64 hexadecimal digits.
  def secret(name : String) -> Secret.T {
    Secret.seal("0303030303030303030303030303030303030303030303030303030303030303")
  }
}
